# Design Narrative
# Mechanic: Assign lethal combat damage to two blockers before assigning trample damage to the defending player.
# Forcing: Charging Monstrosaur has exactly five power, the two blockers each require two damage, and the opponent is at one life.
# AI behavior: The opponent has no cards in hand and both creatures are available to block the only attacker.
# Failure modes:
#   WIN   = both blockers receive lethal damage and the remaining point defeats the opponent.
#   LOSE  = combat resolves without the required trample assignment.
#   TIMEOUT = attacker, blocker, or damage-assignment interaction fails to advance.
# Card roles:
#   Charging Monstrosaur — the hasty five-power trample attacker.
#   Grizzly Bears — the first two-toughness blocker.
#   Runeclaw Bear — the second two-toughness blocker.
# Protocol path: DeclareAttackersReq, DeclareBlockersReq, AssignDamageReq, and their correlated responses.

